1
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:41,959
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:57,224
How can Mr. Kang be fine?

3
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:06,649
That was just an accident.

4
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:09,236
I mean, a minor fender bender.

5
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:12,072
A minor collision.

6
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:15,032
Right, a fender bender.

7
00:01:15,033 --> 00:01:16,493
I was just reaching out for this.

8
00:01:17,411 --> 00:01:18,704
The wind blew out of nowhere.

9
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:20,831
Exactly.

10
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:23,458
It flew off. I don't know why this...

11
00:01:26,378 --> 00:01:29,047
Then again, he's clearly
not inexperienced like me.

12
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:32,301
Well, then.

13
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:36,304
Get home safe.

14
00:01:36,305 --> 00:01:38,932
Oh, okay. You too.

15
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:43,687
Thank you for today.

16
00:01:45,022 --> 00:01:46,023
Good night.

17
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:54,656
Am I the only one shaken up?

18
00:02:01,288 --> 00:02:03,457
That was just an accident.

19
00:02:03,915 --> 00:02:06,126
I mean, a minor fender bender.

20
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:08,170
A minor collision.

21
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:11,632
That was

22
00:02:12,215 --> 00:02:13,717
my very first kiss.

23
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:19,014
He's so unfazed.

24
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:20,807
He's such a pro.

25
00:02:27,189 --> 00:02:29,441
Why is my heart racing like this?

26
00:02:36,198 --> 00:02:37,366
CHAN

27
00:02:37,741 --> 00:02:39,910
Da-reum, did you make it home okay?

28
00:02:49,586 --> 00:02:50,879
What's wrong with me?

29
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:56,176
Another guy friend...

30
00:02:58,929 --> 00:03:01,389
Da-reum, did you have
trouble sleeping last night?

31
00:03:01,390 --> 00:03:03,808
- You look pretty tired.
- I know.

32
00:03:03,809 --> 00:03:04,851
I was

33
00:03:05,185 --> 00:03:06,895
wide awake all night.

34
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:09,522
What kept you so wide awake?

35
00:03:09,523 --> 00:03:11,191
We all have those days.

36
00:03:17,531 --> 00:03:18,740
Hello, sir.

37
00:03:19,116 --> 00:03:20,534
- Good morning.
- Let me through.

38
00:03:21,118 --> 00:03:22,577
- Excuse me.
- Excuse me.

39
00:03:22,828 --> 00:03:24,162
- Excuse me.
- The doors are closing.

40
00:03:37,718 --> 00:03:38,719
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- What is it?

41
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:43,973
- What is it?
- Sorry.

42
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:45,100
- Jeez.
- What...

43
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:48,019
Well, let me...

44
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:51,939
- Excuse me.
- I'm sorry.

45
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,066
Excuse me.

46
00:03:57,028 --> 00:03:59,447
Mr. Kang?

47
00:03:59,448 --> 00:04:01,157
I'm standing behind you.

48
00:04:01,158 --> 00:04:03,200
I'm right here.

49
00:04:03,201 --> 00:04:05,579
It's Lee Min-a. I'm right here.

50
00:04:08,582 --> 00:04:09,833
I guess

51
00:04:11,001 --> 00:04:12,711
it's awkward only for me.

52
00:04:12,878 --> 00:04:15,088
Can't he see me?

53
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,781
THE PALACE WHERE THE WIND RESTS

54
00:04:41,573 --> 00:04:42,865
Chan.

55
00:04:42,866 --> 00:04:44,659
Thank you for the quick decision.

56
00:04:45,202 --> 00:04:48,163
Not at all. I couldn't sleep a wink
after getting the offer yesterday.

57
00:04:48,622 --> 00:04:51,249
It's always been my dream
to work with you.

58
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:53,418
Well, then.

59
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:57,171
I'll reach out after our final talk
with the US co-producers.

60
00:04:57,172 --> 00:04:59,089
I doubt there will be any issues.

61
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:02,010
I see. If you give me the chance,
I won't let you down.

62
00:05:02,511 --> 00:05:05,430
This project will be filmed
entirely on location in LA.

63
00:05:05,806 --> 00:05:07,098
Take a look at this.

64
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,058
Once you're confirmed for the role

65
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:12,144
why don't you head over early
to get a feel for the local vibe?

66
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:14,064
The US team even booked a villa.

67
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:15,898
You could relax
like you're on vacation

68
00:05:15,899 --> 00:05:18,276
and do occasional meetings
or readings.

69
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:21,655
It sounds like a good idea.
It could help with the jet lag too.

70
00:05:23,365 --> 00:05:24,866
I'd love that.

71
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:33,583
From the looks of it,
it's practically confirmed.

72
00:05:34,626 --> 00:05:35,836
Congratulations.

73
00:05:36,837 --> 00:05:40,798
You've always talked about Hollywood,
and now, your dream is coming true.

74
00:05:40,799 --> 00:05:42,425
It's all thanks to you.

75
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:46,012
I'd better sort out
your local schedule first.

76
00:05:49,808 --> 00:05:51,600
Do you think we'll be
in the States for a while?

77
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:53,854
Probably. It's an all-location shoot.

78
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:57,274
But it'll definitely make
your career skyrocket.

79
00:06:02,237 --> 00:06:03,571
DA-REUM, DID YOU MAKE IT HOME OKAY?

80
00:06:03,572 --> 00:06:06,283
DA-REUM:
YES, I'M HOME SAFE. GET SOME REST!

81
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:10,036
Are you dating someone?

82
00:06:13,582 --> 00:06:14,583
Chan.

83
00:06:14,833 --> 00:06:16,877
You've had paparazzi on you for days.

84
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:19,504
And this is a crucial time.

85
00:06:27,304 --> 00:06:28,513
I know.

86
00:06:43,445 --> 00:06:44,446
Hello, Mr. Kang.

87
00:06:45,572 --> 00:06:46,573
Hello, Ms. Da-reum.

88
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:50,368
- Are you buying something for Kung?
- Right.

89
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:52,786
Does Jjak like this too?

90
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:54,288
Oh, totally.

91
00:06:54,289 --> 00:06:56,583
The second I grab this,
its eyes change like a hunter.

92
00:06:58,335 --> 00:06:59,836
I guess
I'll have to buy one for each.

93
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:04,173
How come
you aren't working late today?

94
00:07:04,174 --> 00:07:05,633
I work overtime from home these days.

95
00:07:05,634 --> 00:07:07,052
I felt like
Kung was waiting for me all day.

96
00:07:07,886 --> 00:07:08,970
Same here.

97
00:07:11,598 --> 00:07:13,891
Do you want to meet outside?

98
00:07:13,892 --> 00:07:14,975
Sure.

99
00:07:14,976 --> 00:07:15,977
Wait, what?

100
00:07:19,356 --> 00:07:21,441
No, I mean...

101
00:07:22,609 --> 00:07:24,235
For Kung and Jjak.

102
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:26,655
So they can play together.

103
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,532
I see.

104
00:07:32,744 --> 00:07:33,954
That caught me off guard.

105
00:07:58,895 --> 00:07:59,938
Oh, well.

106
00:08:00,772 --> 00:08:02,148
I guess I wasn't the only one.

107
00:08:09,656 --> 00:08:10,949
INCOMING CALL: CHAN

108
00:08:12,909 --> 00:08:14,995
- Just a moment.
- Oh, okay.

109
00:08:24,796 --> 00:08:25,797
Hey.

110
00:08:28,758 --> 00:08:31,386
I was actually going to call you
when I got home.

111
00:08:33,888 --> 00:08:36,474
No, I'm okay.

112
00:08:37,851 --> 00:08:39,728
Yes, I got home safely yesterday.

113
00:08:41,104 --> 00:08:43,230
Oh, how did that important thing go?

114
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:45,608
It went well. Thanks.

115
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:47,402
That's a relief.

116
00:08:47,694 --> 00:08:50,738
Da-reum, there's something
I really need to tell you.

117
00:08:50,739 --> 00:08:52,073
Are you free tomorrow evening?

118
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:54,033
I'll text you the address.

119
00:08:54,034 --> 00:08:55,118
Let's meet after work.

120
00:08:56,953 --> 00:08:57,954
Okay.

121
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:01,833
Oh, and...

122
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:04,001
I'm sorry. I'll call you back later.

123
00:09:04,002 --> 00:09:05,670
- Okay, bye.
- Bye.

124
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:10,925
- Sorry about that.
- It's fine.

125
00:09:17,515 --> 00:09:18,516
Don't tell me

126
00:09:19,601 --> 00:09:22,479
it's that guy from the blind date.

127
00:09:23,104 --> 00:09:24,105
What?

128
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:26,816
Yes, it's him.

129
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,236
How can he call
after ditching you like that?

130
00:09:33,907 --> 00:09:35,033
I guess he felt bad.

131
00:09:37,786 --> 00:09:40,163
If he was going to feel bad,
he shouldn't have left you there.

132
00:09:41,122 --> 00:09:42,499
He's not a celebrity or anything.

133
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:44,709
What could possibly
make him that busy?

134
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:51,049
Beats me.

135
00:09:52,842 --> 00:09:54,094
Do you realize

136
00:09:55,095 --> 00:09:57,097
you just said, "I'm okay" again?

137
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:05,230
Did I do that again?

138
00:10:06,689 --> 00:10:08,399
Whoever he is

139
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:11,694
you don't need to put up
with him that much.

140
00:10:21,371 --> 00:10:22,455
You're right.

141
00:10:24,332 --> 00:10:25,333
To be honest

142
00:10:26,501 --> 00:10:27,794
it wasn't a blind date.

143
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:31,506
I've liked him for a very long time.

144
00:10:37,512 --> 00:10:38,555
But now that

145
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:41,099
I'm actually seeing him...

146
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:47,605
I find myself

147
00:10:48,523 --> 00:10:50,275
accommodating him
even without him asking.

148
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:54,821
I always prioritize his situation
over mine

149
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:57,740
and my own feelings get pushed aside.

150
00:11:03,830 --> 00:11:04,873
I'm honestly

151
00:11:06,124 --> 00:11:07,167
feeling a bit lost.

152
00:11:13,256 --> 00:11:14,382
Then set one rule for yourself.

153
00:11:16,634 --> 00:11:17,677
Ask yourself...

154
00:11:19,846 --> 00:11:22,140
if this relationship
makes you more like yourself

155
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:24,809
or if it makes you

156
00:11:25,852 --> 00:11:27,270
feel smaller.

157
00:11:32,025 --> 00:11:33,318
Whatever choice you make

158
00:11:34,194 --> 00:11:36,029
just make sure it's a choice

159
00:11:37,322 --> 00:11:38,406
that's true to who you are.

160
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:51,085
- The payment is complete.
- All set.

161
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:05,974
It wasn't a blind date.

162
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:10,063
I've liked him for a very long time.

163
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:19,447
I've liked him for a very long time.

164
00:12:19,948 --> 00:12:20,990
She liked him...

165
00:12:22,784 --> 00:12:23,868
for a long time.

166
00:12:24,869 --> 00:12:25,995
It wasn't me.

167
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:29,749
I wasn't the one.

168
00:12:32,043 --> 00:12:34,045
I'll give it a try.

169
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:39,384
I'm going to be myself from now on.

170
00:12:41,219 --> 00:12:43,513
I like you.

171
00:12:44,055 --> 00:12:46,224
I like you.

172
00:12:51,437 --> 00:12:53,106
This is so annoying.

173
00:12:55,566 --> 00:12:56,734
That guy...

174
00:12:58,653 --> 00:13:00,280
Who the heck is he?

175
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:08,453
HELLO, HA-GI
ASK ME ANYTHING YOU WANT

176
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:12,917
MEETING YOUR LONG-TIME CRUSH

177
00:13:15,003 --> 00:13:18,046
MEETING YOUR LONG-TIME CRUSH
AND REALIZING THEY AREN'T

178
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:19,507
ALL THAT

179
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:23,802
- Would you like
- Oh, my goodness.

180
00:13:23,803 --> 00:13:28,349
some helpful information
about your recent search?

181
00:13:38,609 --> 00:13:39,652
All right.

182
00:13:40,403 --> 00:13:41,487
Let's hear it.

183
00:13:41,779 --> 00:13:45,240
It's totally normal to feel let down

184
00:13:45,241 --> 00:13:48,161
when you finally meet someone
you've spent a long time idealizing.

185
00:13:48,453 --> 00:13:51,580
It stems from the gap
between expectation and reality.

186
00:13:51,581 --> 00:13:52,665
Right?

187
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:56,043
It's better to date someone
who actually likes you

188
00:13:56,044 --> 00:13:58,003
than chasing an unrequited love.
Don't you think?

189
00:13:58,004 --> 00:14:00,589
Statistically speaking,
stable relationships are often built

190
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:03,717
not with a long-term crush

191
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:08,890
but with someone close by
who expresses their feelings first.

192
00:14:12,602 --> 00:14:13,811
Someone close by?

193
00:14:14,228 --> 00:14:15,605
Yes, close by.

194
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:24,781
DIY KNOT KEYCHAIN KIT
BY KNOT MASTER IM CHEONG-RIM

195
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:30,912
UNFRAMED: KNOTTING
UNTYING TRADITIONS TO TIE IT ANEW

196
00:14:39,003 --> 00:14:41,130
Great work.
Let's proceed with this plan.

197
00:14:43,508 --> 00:14:46,302
Yes, sir. I'll do my best.

198
00:14:48,805 --> 00:14:49,806
Ms. Nam.

199
00:14:51,224 --> 00:14:52,225
Yes?

200
00:14:53,059 --> 00:14:54,227
Do you have plans tonight?

201
00:14:55,853 --> 00:14:56,854
Excuse me?

202
00:14:57,647 --> 00:14:59,732
Well...

203
00:15:02,110 --> 00:15:04,153
We should get Kung and Jjak

204
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:05,905
together sometime.

205
00:15:08,491 --> 00:15:11,452
But I already have
a prior engagement tonight.

206
00:15:14,247 --> 00:15:16,624
Then let me know when you're free.

207
00:15:17,417 --> 00:15:18,543
Yes, sir.

208
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,305
A prior engagement?

209
00:15:33,057 --> 00:15:34,183
She already has plans?

210
00:15:38,563 --> 00:15:41,189
Could it be with that guy?

211
00:15:41,190 --> 00:15:43,276
I'm sorry. I'll call you back later.

212
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:47,155
No way.

213
00:15:47,447 --> 00:15:48,865
It can't be.

214
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:01,918
Welcome. Right this way, please.

215
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:03,004
Okay, thank you.

216
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:18,519
Sir.

217
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:23,106
- Hi.
- Hello.

218
00:16:23,107 --> 00:16:24,901
Let me know
if you need anything at all.

219
00:16:25,568 --> 00:16:26,736
Thank you.

220
00:16:28,988 --> 00:16:30,031
Why did you want to see me here?

221
00:16:31,407 --> 00:16:32,825
I have something to celebrate.

222
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:36,496
I figured we could do some shopping
and have a date.

223
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:45,712
Why don't you try this on?

224
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:48,174
- This?
- I think it'll look great on you.

225
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:54,263
It's gorgeous.

226
00:17:10,363 --> 00:17:11,364
What do you think?

227
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:13,741
I like it.

228
00:17:14,534 --> 00:17:16,619
You pull off neutral tones
really well.

229
00:17:18,788 --> 00:17:20,039
It looks amazing on you.

230
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:23,709
Try this one too.

231
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:27,088
Oh, I highly doubt
this one will suit me.

232
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:28,839
You never know until you try it on.

233
00:17:58,452 --> 00:17:59,579
Looks weird, doesn't it?

234
00:17:59,912 --> 00:18:01,122
Not at all.

235
00:18:01,414 --> 00:18:02,498
You look beautiful in it.

236
00:18:04,959 --> 00:18:08,004
I hardly wear clothes like this.

237
00:18:08,296 --> 00:18:09,964
That's exactly why I like it.

238
00:18:10,381 --> 00:18:12,633
It's nice to see
this style suits you.

239
00:18:14,802 --> 00:18:16,012
Da-reum, come here.

240
00:18:31,444 --> 00:18:33,321
This would be a great outfit for LA.

241
00:18:34,905 --> 00:18:35,990
LA?

242
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:38,367
Yes.

243
00:18:39,619 --> 00:18:42,204
So it's practically confirmed.

244
00:18:43,164 --> 00:18:45,249
Working with Director Park Chan-dong!

245
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:48,002
That's incredible.

246
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:50,504
They're still confirming the details.

247
00:18:51,464 --> 00:18:53,549
But I wanted you
to be the first to know.

248
00:18:54,008 --> 00:18:55,509
It's all thanks to your support.

249
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:57,637
- Thank you, Da-reum.
- Not at all.

250
00:18:58,512 --> 00:18:59,930
I'm so happy for you.

251
00:19:08,272 --> 00:19:09,398
Does that mean

252
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:13,319
the shoot will take place
in the States?

253
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:14,862
Yes.

254
00:19:16,656 --> 00:19:19,867
We begin production in LA
early next year.

255
00:19:21,243 --> 00:19:22,995
The exact dates
aren't set yet, though.

256
00:19:24,497 --> 00:19:25,539
I guess...

257
00:19:26,582 --> 00:19:28,668
I won't see you for a while.

258
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:40,304
Why don't you come with me?

259
00:19:42,390 --> 00:19:43,474
Pardon?

260
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:46,477
They're providing
a car and a place for me there.

261
00:19:47,061 --> 00:19:50,064
You could study fashion
while I'm filming.

262
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:51,565
Then we wouldn't have to be apart.

263
00:19:54,235 --> 00:19:55,444
What about the company?

264
00:19:56,362 --> 00:19:58,114
We can work that out.

265
00:19:58,781 --> 00:20:00,699
A lot of people
work remotely these days.

266
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:03,411
Building experience there
could be better for you.

267
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:07,415
You'd love it.

268
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:11,335
LA is full
of fashion shows and brands.

269
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:19,218
That does sound nice.

270
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:21,095
In that sense

271
00:20:21,679 --> 00:20:23,139
I picked one for you too.

272
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:33,566
I actually have
something for you too.

273
00:20:34,442 --> 00:20:35,568
What is it?

274
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:54,754
A cardholder?

275
00:20:55,671 --> 00:20:59,425
Yes, I made it myself
at a leather workshop.

276
00:21:00,009 --> 00:21:01,302
This is really well-made.

277
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:03,179
It's too precious to use.

278
00:21:06,015 --> 00:21:07,141
Thanks.

279
00:21:29,747 --> 00:21:30,831
LA...

280
00:21:42,927 --> 00:21:44,594
Whatever choice you make

281
00:21:44,595 --> 00:21:47,389
just make sure it's a choice
that's true to who you are.

282
00:22:04,532 --> 00:22:06,324
FASHION DIRECTOR NAM DA-REUM!

283
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:08,494
APPELLO'S EMPLOYEE OF THE YEAR!

284
00:22:13,165 --> 00:22:15,000
UNFRAMED: KNOTTING
UNTYING TRADITIONS TO TIE IT ANEW

285
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:27,304
APPELLO BRAND EXPANSION PROPOSAL

286
00:22:56,333 --> 00:22:57,668
Exhale on your way up.

287
00:22:59,086 --> 00:23:01,797
Inhale on your way down.

288
00:23:02,965 --> 00:23:04,800
Come up just a little higher.

289
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:09,346
Hold it right here. One, two.

290
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:11,557
All right.

291
00:23:11,849 --> 00:23:13,726
We're done for today.

292
00:23:15,311 --> 00:23:16,812
Please tidy up your space.

293
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:18,230
Okay.

294
00:23:19,648 --> 00:23:22,568
- Great work.
- Thank you so much.

295
00:23:25,779 --> 00:23:26,780
Well...

296
00:23:30,618 --> 00:23:32,452
Mr. Min-woo, will you come

297
00:23:32,453 --> 00:23:34,121
to the last lesson
of the day next time?

298
00:23:37,917 --> 00:23:40,544
I'm pretty sure she gave me a sign.

299
00:23:43,047 --> 00:23:44,298
Was I wrong?

300
00:23:56,727 --> 00:23:59,395
Thank you for the last session today.

301
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:02,607
- You too.
- Right.

302
00:24:02,608 --> 00:24:05,027
I'll get going, then. Goodbye.

303
00:24:05,653 --> 00:24:06,946
Really, I'm leaving.

304
00:24:09,198 --> 00:24:10,574
- Mr. Min-woo.
- Yes?

305
00:24:10,950 --> 00:24:12,492
We should head out together.

306
00:24:12,493 --> 00:24:15,579
Right? We're grabbing a bite, right?

307
00:24:15,913 --> 00:24:17,581
- Shall we?
- Let's go.

308
00:24:21,377 --> 00:24:22,962
Wow, that looks so good.

309
00:24:23,963 --> 00:24:26,674
- You must be starving.
- Thank you.

310
00:24:26,924 --> 00:24:28,257
Today's session was tough, wasn't it?

311
00:24:28,258 --> 00:24:30,260
Not at all. It was a breeze.

312
00:24:31,095 --> 00:24:32,346
Thank you.

313
00:24:34,223 --> 00:24:36,183
You must be pretty extroverted

314
00:24:36,433 --> 00:24:38,102
to hit on someone
at a place like this.

315
00:24:38,352 --> 00:24:39,602
How did you get here?

316
00:24:39,603 --> 00:24:41,938
- I took a bus.
- Then on your way back

317
00:24:41,939 --> 00:24:43,524
you can take a chance on me.

318
00:24:44,984 --> 00:24:46,276
Oh, you remember that?

319
00:24:49,113 --> 00:24:50,406
That was a first for me.

320
00:24:50,572 --> 00:24:52,448
Seriously.

321
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:55,244
I'm actually a total introvert.
I've never dated anyone.

322
00:24:55,661 --> 00:24:57,788
That day

323
00:24:58,455 --> 00:25:01,291
I fell for you and gathered
the courage for the first time ever.

324
00:25:03,544 --> 00:25:05,962
Is that your go-to pickup line?

325
00:25:05,963 --> 00:25:06,964
Yes.

326
00:25:07,381 --> 00:25:08,924
Just kidding.

327
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:13,345
I tend to ramble a bit
when I'm around someone I like.

328
00:25:13,679 --> 00:25:16,015
- Why?
- To act like I'm not nervous.

329
00:25:18,308 --> 00:25:20,685
What about now, then?

330
00:25:20,686 --> 00:25:21,979
I'm completely like this.

331
00:25:28,235 --> 00:25:30,237
Did that make you laugh?
Guess that's a win.

332
00:25:31,864 --> 00:25:33,031
Anyway

333
00:25:33,032 --> 00:25:35,700
thank you so much for handling
that awful customer the other day.

334
00:25:35,701 --> 00:25:36,910
Don't mention it.

335
00:25:37,703 --> 00:25:40,997
How do you know
all the terms and conditions, though?

336
00:25:40,998 --> 00:25:42,541
No one actually reads those.

337
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:45,127
It's a habit.

338
00:25:45,753 --> 00:25:48,338
The habit of wanting to win
the moment an argument breaks out.

339
00:25:48,797 --> 00:25:51,008
- It's your habit?
- It's just that

340
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:52,968
reading text is part of my job.

341
00:25:57,014 --> 00:25:58,348
Who is he, really?

342
00:25:58,724 --> 00:26:00,017
There's a surprising side to him.

343
00:26:07,816 --> 00:26:09,651
BUCKET LIST FOR LA

344
00:26:11,445 --> 00:26:12,863
It's been updated.

345
00:26:13,822 --> 00:26:15,365
You've added an LA version too.

346
00:26:17,367 --> 00:26:20,370
You've always said making it
to Hollywood was your dream.

347
00:26:20,788 --> 00:26:21,789
Right.

348
00:26:22,289 --> 00:26:24,500
So naturally,
I spent a lot of time picturing it.

349
00:26:25,334 --> 00:26:28,253
We can cross these off together.

350
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:34,968
We'll enjoy the night view
at the observatory

351
00:26:35,677 --> 00:26:37,304
and walk along the beach together.

352
00:26:38,222 --> 00:26:39,389
It's a perfect date itinerary.

353
00:26:49,066 --> 00:26:50,234
Chan.

354
00:26:50,943 --> 00:26:52,444
I have something to say.

355
00:26:54,196 --> 00:26:55,280
Something to say?

356
00:26:57,491 --> 00:26:58,492
You see

357
00:26:59,743 --> 00:27:01,328
I really enjoyed

358
00:27:02,704 --> 00:27:05,457
our time together,
and I definitely had butterflies.

359
00:27:08,544 --> 00:27:09,586
But then...

360
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,173
I don't think

361
00:27:14,299 --> 00:27:15,634
I was being honest.

362
00:27:19,972 --> 00:27:21,014
What do you mean?

363
00:27:21,849 --> 00:27:23,183
With you

364
00:27:24,143 --> 00:27:25,185
and

365
00:27:26,687 --> 00:27:28,147
with myself.

366
00:27:30,232 --> 00:27:31,441
So today

367
00:27:32,109 --> 00:27:33,735
I'm going to stop pretending I'm okay

368
00:27:34,736 --> 00:27:36,405
and just be honest.

369
00:27:47,166 --> 00:27:49,168
I thought if I were with someone I like

370
00:27:50,002 --> 00:27:51,336
I'd be able to share

371
00:27:52,212 --> 00:27:53,255
my feelings with him

372
00:27:53,839 --> 00:27:57,009
by laughing, crying

373
00:27:58,510 --> 00:28:00,971
whining, and even fighting.

374
00:28:02,681 --> 00:28:05,809
But for some reason...

375
00:28:10,022 --> 00:28:11,231
I couldn't easily do that

376
00:28:12,858 --> 00:28:14,526
with you.

377
00:28:19,990 --> 00:28:21,241
I think

378
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:23,702
I still see you

379
00:28:24,328 --> 00:28:25,454
more as an idol

380
00:28:26,288 --> 00:28:27,414
rather than

381
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:30,000
a romantic partner.

382
00:28:34,087 --> 00:28:36,506
I still root for your dreams.

383
00:28:37,549 --> 00:28:39,343
But I have my own dreams
to chase now.

384
00:28:40,510 --> 00:28:42,888
The US sounds great

385
00:28:43,680 --> 00:28:44,848
but I love Appello.

386
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:49,144
I love

387
00:28:50,312 --> 00:28:51,313
the work I do here.

388
00:28:53,106 --> 00:28:54,107
So I'd rather just

389
00:28:55,442 --> 00:28:57,569
stay as Nam Da-reum,
an employee of Appello...

390
00:29:01,907 --> 00:29:03,116
and remain...

391
00:29:07,621 --> 00:29:08,747
your fan.

392
00:29:36,733 --> 00:29:37,985
CHRYSANTHEMUM KNOT
DONGSIMGYEOL KNOT

393
00:29:45,325 --> 00:29:46,868
Here we go.
Nam Da-reum mode activated.

394
00:29:47,411 --> 00:29:49,412
Nam Da-reum mode?
What does that mean?

395
00:29:49,413 --> 00:29:51,414
Remember when we made
the challenge video?

396
00:29:51,415 --> 00:29:53,624
She worked even harder
when she was told to back off.

397
00:29:53,625 --> 00:29:56,962
She thrives when pushed to the brink.
I call it Nam Da-reum mode.

398
00:29:57,587 --> 00:30:02,049
Ms. Da-reum, you aren't being pushed
to the edge again, are you?

399
00:30:02,050 --> 00:30:04,219
Not at all. I just like doing it

400
00:30:04,970 --> 00:30:06,888
because it keeps
my mind from wandering.

401
00:30:11,977 --> 00:30:14,354
What happened to your hand?
Did you injure yourself?

402
00:30:15,439 --> 00:30:17,441
I'm currently fostering a kitten.

403
00:30:18,233 --> 00:30:22,528
I need to find someone to adopt it
but I've been too busy to even try.

404
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:25,656
A cat? I've actually been
preparing to adopt one.

405
00:30:25,657 --> 00:30:27,491
Hold on. Can I see a picture?

406
00:30:27,492 --> 00:30:28,701
- Really?
- Yes.

407
00:30:28,702 --> 00:30:29,870
Just a second.

408
00:30:30,287 --> 00:30:33,623
- Do you like animals?
- Yes, totally.

409
00:30:34,499 --> 00:30:35,751
Me too.

410
00:30:36,418 --> 00:30:37,586
Isn't it adorable?

411
00:30:39,546 --> 00:30:40,755
The name is Jjak.

412
00:30:40,756 --> 00:30:42,131
There are actually two.

413
00:30:42,132 --> 00:30:44,550
Their names are Kung and Jjak,
like a matching beat.

414
00:30:44,551 --> 00:30:47,094
Oh, my gosh. It's adorable.

415
00:30:47,095 --> 00:30:49,472
No joke, I've wanted an orange tabby.

416
00:30:49,473 --> 00:30:51,016
- Are you serious?
- Dead serious.

417
00:30:51,641 --> 00:30:52,934
Here's another one.

418
00:30:54,061 --> 00:30:56,938
- Adorable, right?
- Oh, my. It's so cute.

419
00:31:05,947 --> 00:31:07,656
This is the script
from Director Park Chan-dong.

420
00:31:07,657 --> 00:31:10,660
Chan, your casting is finalized!

421
00:31:13,497 --> 00:31:15,290
THE TARGET: THE LAST AIM

422
00:31:17,542 --> 00:31:20,170
- What is it? You can't believe it?
- What?

423
00:31:20,545 --> 00:31:22,005
No, it's just that
things are going so well.

424
00:31:23,382 --> 00:31:24,965
Is that really your concern?

425
00:31:24,966 --> 00:31:26,967
Wait, all right.
Let's celebrate later.

426
00:31:26,968 --> 00:31:29,303
Since it's all shot in the States,
we've got tons to do.

427
00:31:29,304 --> 00:31:32,765
Clearing schedules, sorting visas,
getting you in shape...

428
00:31:32,766 --> 00:31:34,683
And if you need anything,
just write it down.

429
00:31:34,684 --> 00:31:36,645
Won-bin,
I can't let it end like this.

430
00:31:38,397 --> 00:31:40,107
Chan, where are you going?

431
00:32:00,252 --> 00:32:01,294
Mr. Kang.

432
00:32:04,840 --> 00:32:06,174
You're still here?

433
00:32:07,592 --> 00:32:09,010
I'm going to finish a bit more.

434
00:32:19,980 --> 00:32:22,232
You really don't have to...

435
00:32:25,110 --> 00:32:26,361
Thank you.

436
00:32:31,575 --> 00:32:34,244
No date tonight?

437
00:32:34,870 --> 00:32:35,871
No.

438
00:32:36,705 --> 00:32:39,875
I'm way
too swamped for that right now.

439
00:32:40,125 --> 00:32:41,501
Why are you doing
all this by yourself?

440
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:43,044
I never gave such an order.

441
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:46,381
My coworkers helped out a lot
during the day.

442
00:32:46,631 --> 00:32:49,718
I'm just finishing up what's left.

443
00:32:50,469 --> 00:32:51,803
It must be hard
taking on a major event

444
00:32:52,888 --> 00:32:53,930
all of a sudden.

445
00:32:55,974 --> 00:32:58,685
It's a little overwhelming.

446
00:32:59,144 --> 00:33:03,231
Still, it feels rewarding
to be in charge of something.

447
00:33:14,451 --> 00:33:15,952
You'll learn a lot

448
00:33:17,245 --> 00:33:18,413
from each project you handle.

449
00:33:19,539 --> 00:33:20,540
Right.

450
00:33:21,541 --> 00:33:22,625
Oh, right.

451
00:33:22,626 --> 00:33:25,629
Young-woo said
he wanted to adopt Kung and Jjak.

452
00:33:26,254 --> 00:33:29,549
You're sending them away already?

453
00:33:29,966 --> 00:33:31,926
I'm upset about it a bit too

454
00:33:31,927 --> 00:33:34,471
but it's great for Kung and Jjak.

455
00:33:35,263 --> 00:33:36,431
It is.

456
00:33:37,933 --> 00:33:40,936
I bought Kung lots of toys.

457
00:33:41,436 --> 00:33:42,811
What else did you get?

458
00:33:42,812 --> 00:33:44,689
I said you didn't have to.

459
00:33:45,815 --> 00:33:46,816
Still.

460
00:33:48,193 --> 00:33:49,194
Where did you get them?

461
00:33:49,861 --> 00:33:51,947
From stores and stuff.

462
00:33:58,745 --> 00:34:01,540
Ms. Da-reum?
She's working late today.

463
00:34:58,430 --> 00:34:59,598
Mr. Kang.

464
00:35:00,015 --> 00:35:02,809
Do you remember
what you said to me last time?

465
00:35:04,352 --> 00:35:05,353
What did I say?

466
00:35:06,980 --> 00:35:08,606
That whatever choice I make

467
00:35:08,607 --> 00:35:10,650
I should make sure
I'd be true to who I am.

468
00:35:16,865 --> 00:35:18,158
Thanks to what you said

469
00:35:19,200 --> 00:35:20,452
I could pluck up the courage.

470
00:35:30,003 --> 00:35:31,171
For the first time ever

471
00:35:32,922 --> 00:35:34,257
I was able to be honest.

472
00:35:35,842 --> 00:35:37,594
And I made a choice
that was true to myself.

473
00:35:41,556 --> 00:35:43,016
Thank you, Mr. Kang.

474
00:35:48,063 --> 00:35:50,857
You were just someone
who was always capable

475
00:35:52,609 --> 00:35:53,902
of making that choice.

476
00:36:00,575 --> 00:36:03,870
It seems more like it
now that you put it into words.

477
00:36:08,875 --> 00:36:11,795
She broke it off with that guy, then.

478
00:36:23,056 --> 00:36:25,433
- Ms. Da-reum.
- Yes?

479
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:28,812
I have something to...

480
00:36:29,312 --> 00:36:30,814
I see you're hard at work.

481
00:36:33,316 --> 00:36:34,317
Why are you here?

482
00:36:34,943 --> 00:36:37,362
I heard you stayed behind
to prepare for the pop-up.

483
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:40,198
Is this the DIY kit?

484
00:36:41,491 --> 00:36:42,617
Yes, Director.

485
00:36:49,040 --> 00:36:50,875
How is it made? Teach me.

486
00:36:53,336 --> 00:36:54,337
Take a seat.

487
00:37:09,436 --> 00:37:12,646
You work so fast, Director.

488
00:37:12,647 --> 00:37:15,525
I once signed
over 1,000 albums in a day.

489
00:37:16,025 --> 00:37:17,110
This is nothing.

490
00:37:17,736 --> 00:37:18,945
Fold it properly.

491
00:37:19,487 --> 00:37:21,239
Focus on the detail,
not just the speed.

492
00:37:22,365 --> 00:37:23,700
Yes, boss.

493
00:37:28,997 --> 00:37:30,206
Ms. Da-reum. Check this.

494
00:37:38,047 --> 00:37:40,592
So, Ms. Da-reum.

495
00:37:41,092 --> 00:37:43,928
Who are you a better match with
between us two?

496
00:37:45,930 --> 00:37:46,973
Sorry?

497
00:37:47,766 --> 00:37:48,892
Why do you want to know that?

498
00:37:50,185 --> 00:37:52,020
Everyone has a type.

499
00:38:03,865 --> 00:38:06,534
I'm still new, so I can't say.

500
00:38:06,910 --> 00:38:09,704
And you two are so different.

501
00:38:14,125 --> 00:38:16,920
What a safe, political reply.

502
00:38:22,258 --> 00:38:25,929
I just wanted to know
if you were leaning toward anyone.

503
00:39:19,065 --> 00:39:20,108
We need to talk.

504
00:39:24,737 --> 00:39:25,822
Did you really

505
00:39:26,656 --> 00:39:28,116
come here today about work?

506
00:39:29,158 --> 00:39:30,201
Why?

507
00:39:30,785 --> 00:39:32,370
And when you came
to Master Im's place?

508
00:39:36,791 --> 00:39:38,543
Because this is an important project.

509
00:39:40,253 --> 00:39:41,254
Do you

510
00:39:43,298 --> 00:39:44,507
like Ms. Da-reum?

511
00:39:52,307 --> 00:39:53,349
I do like her.

512
00:39:58,479 --> 00:39:59,647
She's my favorite employee.

513
00:40:01,482 --> 00:40:03,818
Who wouldn't like someone
who works so hard?

514
00:40:04,277 --> 00:40:05,320
Only as an employee?

515
00:40:06,821 --> 00:40:08,156
What do you want me to say?

516
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:11,159
You tried to go after her just now.

517
00:40:15,496 --> 00:40:16,664
What about you, then?

518
00:40:17,957 --> 00:40:19,876
Are you protecting your employee

519
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:21,502
or are you keeping me in check?

520
00:40:28,134 --> 00:40:29,177
You won't answer either.

521
00:40:33,848 --> 00:40:35,391
Once you decide to become honest

522
00:40:39,228 --> 00:40:40,563
so will I.

523
00:41:07,048 --> 00:41:08,132
Ms. Da-reum.

524
00:41:09,133 --> 00:41:11,594
Who are you a better match with
between us two?

525
00:41:14,722 --> 00:41:17,183
I want to start dating you.

526
00:41:17,725 --> 00:41:18,726
Da-reum.

527
00:41:19,435 --> 00:41:21,521
I'm sorry for that day.

528
00:41:21,813 --> 00:41:23,982
Please don't mind me.

529
00:41:24,524 --> 00:41:26,525
I feel bad
to send you home like this.

530
00:41:26,526 --> 00:41:28,277
I'm really fine.

531
00:41:28,987 --> 00:41:30,405
But you're not okay.

532
00:41:30,947 --> 00:41:33,950
At least, in front of me
you can say it's not okay.

533
00:41:41,541 --> 00:41:42,542
I just wanted to know

534
00:41:42,875 --> 00:41:44,836
if you were leaning toward anyone.

535
00:41:51,342 --> 00:41:52,927
Coming!

536
00:41:53,219 --> 00:41:54,720
Hi, thank you.

537
00:41:54,721 --> 00:41:56,431
Enjoy the food and have a happy day.

538
00:41:59,225 --> 00:42:00,935
Have a happy day.

539
00:42:01,978 --> 00:42:04,479
I hope my voice brings you
a small piece of happiness

540
00:42:04,480 --> 00:42:06,190
every single day.

541
00:42:06,941 --> 00:42:09,068
This is Roy from D.N.X signing off.

542
00:42:24,042 --> 00:42:26,294
That was most definitely Roy's voice.

543
00:42:45,938 --> 00:42:47,690
I wanted to have kalguksu today.

544
00:42:47,982 --> 00:42:49,566
We failed yet again today.

545
00:42:49,567 --> 00:42:51,902
When will we ever get to eat there?

546
00:42:51,903 --> 00:42:54,488
We don't stand a chance
unless we take the morning off

547
00:42:54,489 --> 00:42:55,573
to wait in line.

548
00:42:56,491 --> 00:42:58,617
I really wanted to try out
Kalguksu Jip.

549
00:42:58,618 --> 00:43:00,077
Me too.

550
00:43:00,078 --> 00:43:02,788
Shall we go to the rooftop
for a stroll to digest our lunch?

551
00:43:02,789 --> 00:43:04,122
- Good idea.
- Isn't it?

552
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:05,792
I have some work to get back to.

553
00:43:06,209 --> 00:43:08,127
Ms. Min-a, shall we go, then?

554
00:43:08,461 --> 00:43:09,586
Yes, sure.

555
00:43:09,587 --> 00:43:10,671
- See you later.
- Bye.

556
00:43:11,047 --> 00:43:12,507
See you in a bit.

557
00:43:17,804 --> 00:43:19,763
You didn't go out to lunch, Ms. Seo?

558
00:43:19,764 --> 00:43:21,015
I'm leaving now.

559
00:43:21,641 --> 00:43:23,100
I see you had an early lunch.

560
00:43:23,101 --> 00:43:24,936
- Yes. Enjoy your meal.
- Thanks.

561
00:43:45,414 --> 00:43:47,375
Did the cleaning lady come by?

562
00:43:59,470 --> 00:44:01,930
It looks like you're running away.

563
00:44:01,931 --> 00:44:03,890
Why's there so much stuff for a cat?

564
00:44:03,891 --> 00:44:05,518
I kept buying stuff.

565
00:44:10,022 --> 00:44:13,526
Here, hand over the cat

566
00:44:14,527 --> 00:44:15,987
and tell her how you feel.

567
00:44:18,239 --> 00:44:19,573
What are you on about?

568
00:44:19,574 --> 00:44:22,242
Don't miss out
on an opportunity like this.

569
00:44:22,243 --> 00:44:24,287
- Good luck over there.
- What the heck?

570
00:44:24,829 --> 00:44:25,872
Go on home.

571
00:44:27,874 --> 00:44:30,501
Good luck, okay? Do your thing.

572
00:44:32,753 --> 00:44:33,796
I'm leaving.

573
00:44:38,676 --> 00:44:39,927
How I feel?

574
00:44:40,928 --> 00:44:42,221
Tell her how you feel.

575
00:44:44,891 --> 00:44:46,684
Someone close by.

576
00:45:04,076 --> 00:45:05,119
Hang on.

577
00:45:08,122 --> 00:45:10,166
I'll come by around 8 p.m.

578
00:45:10,666 --> 00:45:13,461
Great. Kung and Jjak
will meet at last.

579
00:45:14,378 --> 00:45:17,089
There's a lot of stuff,
so I'll come to your place.

580
00:45:17,465 --> 00:45:18,716
I'm setting off now.

581
00:45:19,926 --> 00:45:21,510
He's so considerate.

582
00:45:31,145 --> 00:45:32,313
See you again, Da-reum.

583
00:45:37,026 --> 00:45:38,277
If Mr. Kang sees this...

584
00:45:39,070 --> 00:45:40,112
No!

585
00:45:56,796 --> 00:45:57,797
Am I done?

586
00:46:17,441 --> 00:46:18,776
Tell her how you feel.

587
00:46:23,906 --> 00:46:26,033
Hello, Kung.

588
00:46:29,704 --> 00:46:31,205
Wait here.

589
00:46:32,248 --> 00:46:34,583
That must've been heavy.
Thank you, Mr. Kang.

590
00:46:39,588 --> 00:46:40,673
Wear these.

591
00:46:42,800 --> 00:46:45,469
- The thing is...
- Yes?

592
00:46:47,638 --> 00:46:49,598
It's my first time
visiting a lady's home.

593
00:46:51,309 --> 00:46:53,643
I hope you don't mind the intrusion.

594
00:46:53,644 --> 00:46:55,896
It's fine. Make yourself at home.

595
00:47:04,822 --> 00:47:06,365
You can take your time.

596
00:47:24,050 --> 00:47:25,301
Have some tea.

597
00:47:26,802 --> 00:47:27,887
Thanks.

598
00:47:40,232 --> 00:47:41,609
Jjak.

599
00:47:42,360 --> 00:47:46,738
Listen. Kung is here to see you.

600
00:47:46,739 --> 00:47:48,573
They've grown a lot.

601
00:47:48,574 --> 00:47:51,202
You think so?
Isn't Kung the same size?

602
00:47:52,119 --> 00:47:53,120
Kung is...

603
00:47:55,664 --> 00:47:56,832
Where's Kung?

604
00:47:58,793 --> 00:47:59,877
Kung.

605
00:48:03,881 --> 00:48:05,216
When did it get in there?

606
00:48:07,301 --> 00:48:08,386
I'll go get Kung.

607
00:48:09,762 --> 00:48:12,556
- Kung.
- What?

608
00:48:14,183 --> 00:48:16,185
You wait here. Oh, no.

609
00:48:16,435 --> 00:48:17,603
Kung?

610
00:48:21,315 --> 00:48:22,691
- Wait!
- Scared me.

611
00:48:23,692 --> 00:48:26,111
You can't go in there. Not ever.

612
00:48:26,112 --> 00:48:27,113
It's my secret...

613
00:48:29,657 --> 00:48:31,200
It's my underwear closet.

614
00:48:33,160 --> 00:48:34,286
I apologize.

615
00:48:34,703 --> 00:48:35,704
Then...

616
00:48:37,206 --> 00:48:39,333
I won't even take a peek.

617
00:48:46,632 --> 00:48:48,299
Sit over there and wait.

618
00:48:48,300 --> 00:48:51,387
- I'll get Kung and join you.
- Okay.

619
00:48:52,012 --> 00:48:55,433
- I don't see a thing right now.
- Good.

620
00:49:00,312 --> 00:49:03,898
SHINING BRIGHT, LEE CHAN

621
00:49:03,899 --> 00:49:05,609
That was
the biggest crisis of my life.

622
00:49:11,407 --> 00:49:14,994
I can't hide that I'm Chan's fan
from Mr. Kang forever.

623
00:49:16,162 --> 00:49:17,163
Should I just

624
00:49:17,913 --> 00:49:19,915
tell him the truth?

625
00:49:25,212 --> 00:49:26,505
They really recognize each other.

626
00:49:27,339 --> 00:49:28,799
Isn't that fascinating?

627
00:49:28,966 --> 00:49:31,342
You said they fought
and ate each other's food

628
00:49:31,343 --> 00:49:32,595
when they were together.

629
00:49:34,930 --> 00:49:38,559
They fight when they're together
and miss each other when apart.

630
00:49:40,769 --> 00:49:42,021
It must be like that

631
00:49:43,522 --> 00:49:44,565
for people...

632
00:49:47,860 --> 00:49:48,986
and for cats, too.

633
00:49:56,494 --> 00:49:58,704
Yes. Now is the time.

634
00:50:00,331 --> 00:50:02,166
Mr. Kang.

635
00:50:03,292 --> 00:50:06,754
The truth is...

636
00:50:07,963 --> 00:50:09,048
Yes?

637
00:50:10,674 --> 00:50:11,800
So...

638
00:50:13,302 --> 00:50:15,554
- For a long time...
- Excuse me.

639
00:50:18,724 --> 00:50:19,808
Yes, hello.

640
00:50:20,392 --> 00:50:23,479
I'm not at home.
I'll check when I get back.

641
00:50:26,315 --> 00:50:28,776
- What were you about to say?
- What?

642
00:50:32,821 --> 00:50:36,325
Oh, I was going to thank you
for bringing Kung.

643
00:50:38,327 --> 00:50:39,620
I should thank you.

644
00:50:40,287 --> 00:50:41,830
I did bring Kung over

645
00:50:42,581 --> 00:50:44,124
but I got to see Jjak again.

646
00:50:47,211 --> 00:50:48,837
And I got to see you again.

647
00:50:51,423 --> 00:50:52,508
It's nice.

648
00:51:11,735 --> 00:51:13,028
Look at the time.

649
00:51:14,071 --> 00:51:16,407
- I should go.
- That's so sudden.

650
00:51:17,575 --> 00:51:18,784
You should rest.

651
00:51:19,952 --> 00:51:22,079
Kung, I'm leaving.

652
00:51:23,706 --> 00:51:25,248
I'll see you at work, then.

653
00:51:25,249 --> 00:51:28,836
- Drive home safely, Mr. Kang.
- Bye.

654
00:51:41,724 --> 00:51:42,975
Did she get the message?

655
00:51:53,027 --> 00:51:54,486
I got to see you again.

656
00:51:55,446 --> 00:51:56,447
It's nice.

657
00:51:57,948 --> 00:51:59,700
"I got to see you again.

658
00:52:00,784 --> 00:52:02,036
It's nice."

659
00:52:05,873 --> 00:52:07,082
I agree.

660
00:52:18,761 --> 00:52:20,095
Yes, that's right.

661
00:52:20,763 --> 00:52:23,557
How did you get the company photos?

662
00:52:24,767 --> 00:52:27,686
Oh, really? No wonder.

663
00:52:28,562 --> 00:52:30,147
I look forward to your article.

664
00:52:35,819 --> 00:52:37,195
- Hello.
- Hello.

665
00:52:37,196 --> 00:52:39,073
- Hi. Sit over here, please.
- Hello.

666
00:52:42,326 --> 00:52:44,203
- I'll get everything ready.
- Okay.

667
00:52:50,084 --> 00:52:53,170
I heard you'll be working
with Director Park Chan-dong.

668
00:52:53,420 --> 00:52:56,340
- I'm really happy for you.
- Thanks.

669
00:52:58,717 --> 00:53:01,387
I'm working
on a global project of my own.

670
00:53:01,887 --> 00:53:02,930
We're filming in the US.

671
00:53:04,807 --> 00:53:06,475
- In the US?
- Yes.

672
00:53:07,184 --> 00:53:08,519
What interesting timing.

673
00:53:09,853 --> 00:53:13,190
It looks like
we're meant to keep crossing paths.

674
00:53:24,493 --> 00:53:26,077
They're so adorable.

675
00:53:26,078 --> 00:53:29,289
I couldn't sleep for days.
They're so cute.

676
00:53:30,207 --> 00:53:31,333
Oh, my gosh.

677
00:53:32,584 --> 00:53:33,836
- Hi.
- Hello.

678
00:53:39,299 --> 00:53:40,426
You're leaving together?

679
00:53:41,135 --> 00:53:44,138
Yes. He's coming by to get the cats.

680
00:53:44,513 --> 00:53:45,723
I'm on my way home, too.

681
00:53:46,223 --> 00:53:47,266
I'll tag along.

682
00:53:48,517 --> 00:53:49,768
I'll drive you there.

683
00:53:50,978 --> 00:53:53,856
- We're headed in the same direction.
- I'd like that.

684
00:54:30,392 --> 00:54:33,937
Kung and Jjak. Look after yourselves.

685
00:54:34,897 --> 00:54:36,899
Don't forget me, okay?

686
00:54:38,776 --> 00:54:41,653
- Bye.
- Take care.

687
00:54:45,115 --> 00:54:48,159
I'll take really good care
of Kung and Jjak.

688
00:54:48,160 --> 00:54:50,829
Mr. Kang. Thank you so much
for helping with the luggage.

689
00:54:52,498 --> 00:54:53,707
Bye, Young-woo.

690
00:54:54,124 --> 00:54:56,835
If you don't mind me asking,
do you think...

691
00:54:58,378 --> 00:54:59,671
Never mind.

692
00:55:02,341 --> 00:55:03,926
By any chance...

693
00:55:11,266 --> 00:55:14,018
Wouldn't it be a shame
to part like this?

694
00:55:14,019 --> 00:55:16,020
Since we're coworkers

695
00:55:16,021 --> 00:55:17,856
how about some coffee
with Mr. Kang too?

696
00:55:19,608 --> 00:55:20,776
That's a no.

697
00:55:21,276 --> 00:55:23,986
Cats get very stressed out
in unfamiliar settings.

698
00:55:23,987 --> 00:55:26,197
They need their owner
on their first day.

699
00:55:26,198 --> 00:55:28,658
Yes, right, of course.
You're the CEO for a reason.

700
00:55:28,659 --> 00:55:31,036
- Let's pass on it today.
- Yes. Maybe next time.

701
00:55:31,995 --> 00:55:34,081
Go on home
and help the cats settle in.

702
00:55:34,498 --> 00:55:36,333
I'll do that. Goodbye.

703
00:55:36,875 --> 00:55:37,876
Bye.

704
00:55:39,962 --> 00:55:41,045
Ms. Da-reum.

705
00:55:41,046 --> 00:55:42,881
Let's hang out soon.

706
00:55:43,173 --> 00:55:44,550
Without Mr. Kang.

707
00:55:46,176 --> 00:55:47,302
Sounds good.

708
00:55:52,099 --> 00:55:55,519
Kung, Jjak, live happily ever after.

709
00:55:56,728 --> 00:55:58,355
Look after each other.

710
00:56:02,526 --> 00:56:03,610
Don't fight.

711
00:56:11,159 --> 00:56:13,745
Ms. Da-reum. Are you crying?

712
00:56:15,998 --> 00:56:17,040
No.

713
00:56:18,792 --> 00:56:21,336
I guess I got attached to them.

714
00:56:26,633 --> 00:56:27,718
I think

715
00:56:29,136 --> 00:56:30,637
I got more attached.

716
00:56:35,183 --> 00:56:37,728
I liked asking each day
if they'd eaten.

717
00:56:39,855 --> 00:56:41,440
The weird photos too.

718
00:56:43,734 --> 00:56:45,027
I looked forward to them.

719
00:56:48,614 --> 00:56:49,615
Yes.

720
00:56:50,574 --> 00:56:51,783
Now the cats are gone.

721
00:56:55,913 --> 00:56:57,205
I have no reason to contact you.

722
00:57:03,837 --> 00:57:04,880
Well...

723
00:57:18,226 --> 00:57:19,603
What's wrong with me?

724
00:57:26,610 --> 00:57:27,778
Shall we have dinner together?

725
00:57:29,571 --> 00:57:30,864
It would be a shame
to part like this.

726
00:57:35,410 --> 00:57:37,120
Sure. I'd like that.

727
00:57:38,872 --> 00:57:39,915
- Let's go.
- Okay.

728
00:57:45,712 --> 00:57:47,505
Next. Come on in.

729
00:57:47,506 --> 00:57:51,009
I really wanted to try this place.
How did you hear about it?

730
00:57:52,344 --> 00:57:53,345
Well...

731
00:57:53,720 --> 00:57:54,804
KALGUKSU JIP

732
00:57:54,805 --> 00:57:57,224
- I heard they're famous.
- They are.

733
00:57:58,475 --> 00:58:00,685
We failed yet again today.

734
00:58:00,686 --> 00:58:02,729
When will we ever get to eat there?

735
00:58:04,106 --> 00:58:06,440
I really wanted to try out
Kalguksu Jip.

736
00:58:06,441 --> 00:58:08,484
- Me, too.
- Kalguksu?

737
00:58:08,485 --> 00:58:09,568
WHAT ARE YOU LOOKING FOR?

738
00:58:09,569 --> 00:58:13,073
Famous kalguksu places nearby.

739
00:58:15,951 --> 00:58:17,285
I found it.

740
00:58:23,208 --> 00:58:26,043
- You wanted to try this that much?
- Yes.

741
00:58:26,044 --> 00:58:28,463
They don't take reservations,
so it's really hard to get in.

742
00:58:30,465 --> 00:58:31,466
Over here.

743
00:58:36,013 --> 00:58:37,097
Sorry about that.

744
00:58:39,641 --> 00:58:40,642
Stand on this side.

745
00:58:41,768 --> 00:58:42,769
Thank you.

746
00:58:54,364 --> 00:58:56,408
Two bowls of kalguksu.

747
00:58:57,826 --> 00:58:59,995
- Thank you.
- Enjoy yourselves.

748
00:59:00,996 --> 00:59:02,788
Look at the color of the broth.

749
00:59:02,789 --> 00:59:04,666
There's no way this isn't good.

750
00:59:05,042 --> 00:59:06,752
Okay, just a moment, please.

751
00:59:08,003 --> 00:59:10,714
- More pickled radish, please.
- Leave that here.

752
00:59:14,760 --> 00:59:15,802
What is it?

753
00:59:16,887 --> 00:59:18,263
Do you not like it?

754
00:59:27,439 --> 00:59:29,566
This tastes amazing.

755
00:59:29,900 --> 00:59:32,486
Right? They're famous for a reason.

756
00:59:32,861 --> 00:59:34,196
Let's dig in.

757
00:59:44,664 --> 00:59:45,707
It's good.

758
00:59:49,252 --> 00:59:50,420
That was awesome.

759
00:59:50,962 --> 00:59:53,924
- It was worth the wait, wasn't it?
- Yes.

760
00:59:57,511 --> 00:59:59,554
Mr. Kang, look at that.

761
01:00:00,138 --> 01:00:01,347
STAR GAME ARCADE

762
01:00:01,348 --> 01:00:02,599
Doesn't that look like Jjak?

763
01:00:03,016 --> 01:00:07,228
That expression
and the light-lipped mouth.

764
01:00:07,229 --> 01:00:08,396
It's totally Jjak.

765
01:00:08,897 --> 01:00:09,940
How cute.

766
01:00:11,399 --> 01:00:12,776
- Do you want it?
- What?

767
01:00:15,028 --> 01:00:16,780
Mr. Kang.

768
01:00:18,198 --> 01:00:19,449
INSERT COIN HERE

769
01:00:39,886 --> 01:00:41,805
Yes, I got it.

770
01:00:50,689 --> 01:00:51,690
Darn it!

771
01:00:55,610 --> 01:00:57,820
Mr. Kang, that's enough.

772
01:00:57,821 --> 01:01:00,322
Watching you
was more than enough fun.

773
01:01:00,323 --> 01:01:03,368
- No, I see the pattern now.
- What?

774
01:01:05,287 --> 01:01:07,288
The claw's pressure is consistent

775
01:01:07,289 --> 01:01:09,833
but if you look carefully,
it's skewed slightly to the left.

776
01:01:10,083 --> 01:01:11,084
I failed just now

777
01:01:12,252 --> 01:01:13,461
because the angle was wrong.

778
01:01:16,173 --> 01:01:19,926
Mr. Kang. Why are you
so serious about this?

779
01:01:21,970 --> 01:01:23,138
We have a goal.

780
01:01:23,847 --> 01:01:24,848
We want Jjak.

781
01:01:25,765 --> 01:01:27,267
It's time to end it.

782
01:01:46,578 --> 01:01:49,623
You selected the angle
and chose a strategy.

783
01:01:49,873 --> 01:01:51,625
You looked almost professional.

784
01:01:53,293 --> 01:01:55,378
I wanted to get you
the Jjak lookalike.

785
01:01:56,421 --> 01:01:58,839
- Sorry.
- Don't be.

786
01:01:58,840 --> 01:02:00,759
This is more than cute.

787
01:02:02,177 --> 01:02:03,511
You were cute, too.

788
01:02:14,731 --> 01:02:15,774
I had...

789
01:02:17,442 --> 01:02:18,443
fun today.

790
01:02:20,278 --> 01:02:21,321
So did I.

791
01:02:22,072 --> 01:02:23,073
Also...

792
01:02:24,574 --> 01:02:25,951
Kung and Jjak left

793
01:02:27,410 --> 01:02:28,662
but you can still contact me

794
01:02:30,247 --> 01:02:31,414
for no reason.

795
01:02:34,417 --> 01:02:35,460
I liked

796
01:02:36,211 --> 01:02:37,796
listening to whatever...

797
01:02:40,215 --> 01:02:41,299
you had to say.

798
01:02:54,771 --> 01:02:55,772
Listen.

799
01:02:57,941 --> 01:02:59,276
Not as your CEO...

800
01:03:01,695 --> 01:03:02,862
but as Kang Ha-gi...

801
01:03:07,534 --> 01:03:08,535
I want to...

802
01:03:17,502 --> 01:03:18,586
Excuse me.

803
01:03:21,673 --> 01:03:23,383
TEAM MANAGER KIM MI-YOUNG
REPORTER PARK MIN-HA

804
01:03:30,598 --> 01:03:32,641
- Hi, Seul-a.
- Hey!

805
01:03:32,642 --> 01:03:35,520
There's a scandal about you and Chan.

806
01:03:37,105 --> 01:03:40,066
There are articles
with photos of you two together.

807
01:03:42,235 --> 01:03:43,236
What?

808
01:03:52,203 --> 01:03:53,913
THEY SEEMED
TO BE ENJOYING THEIR DATE

809
01:04:11,014 --> 01:04:12,098
Mr. Kang.

810
